    "# Granite 4.1 3B - pinned column, floors 0-25 and 31-39 (Kaggle)\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the cloud half of the depth column. The laptop already ran channels\n",
    "2941-2956 on **L26-L30** (`grid_L*_3h.jsonl`, bf16).\n",
    "This notebook runs the *identical* cell definition on **35 other floors**\n",
    "(0-25 and 31-39), so the whole 40-floor axis becomes one\n",
    "comparable column at fixed tiles.\n",
    "\n",
    "| axis | value |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| tiles | 2941..2956 (16 channels) |\n",
    "| probes | `hello` / `what is your name` / `do you like humans` |\n",
    "| doses | 4 5 6, both signs |\n",
    "| cap | `max_new=45`, greedy |\n",
    "| dtype | **float16** (P100 has no fast bf16); every row records `dtype` |\n",
    "| budget | 2700s per floor, ~35 floors |\n",
    "| expected | 10,080 rows, ~6.4 h at the measured 0.44 rows/s |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Floors 26-30 are excluded on purpose** - the laptop already owns them in bf16 at\n",
